From 1045ea22ffc35d68521c40febe28fe5f235a2457 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
Date: Sun, 15 Nov 2026 06:24:14 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 35/35] fix(harbor_agent): Terminus-2 ends the episode after 8
 consecutive truncations

On a reply that hits max_tokens with nothing salvageable (always, with the
json parser), Harbor 0.25's Terminus2._query_llm appends it plus "ERROR!!
NONE of the actions ..." and calls itself again, with no limit. In jobs
5350472 and 5355345, 3 trials each looped 320 times until Python's
recursion limit, ran 620-1125 s, came back without a reward and held up
the step.

Terminus2NemoGym counts the nesting of _query_llm, which only recurses on
such a reply, and at max_consecutive_truncations (default 8, None: no
limit) makes no further model call: a placeholder unwinds the chain
without an exception (each level's @retry would retry one), and the
outermost call raises TruncationLoopError. run() already turns that into
a normal return, so Harbor runs the verifier and the rollout gets a real
reward, as when the context overflows.

Default 8: in those two jobs (512 trials) 95% of truncation runs had 1-3
replies, no trial with a run of 6 or more got a reward above 0, and every
run of 10 or more ended in reward 0, a recursion error or a timeout.

The kwarg joins SHARED_AGENT_KWARGS, so OpenCode and mini drop it when an
env yaml sets it.

Signed-off-by: Philip Mueller <claude@philipmueller.ch>
